        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para><computeroutput>Inst</computeroutput> uses or touches memory. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Return an <ref refid="namespacellvm_1_1_calling_conv_1abdf8cf606905c10634e831390981b0ed" kindref="member">ID</ref> describing the memory state at <computeroutput>Inst</computeroutput> such that if getMemoryUseOrder(I1) == getMemoryUseOrder(I2), the exact same memory operations happen after I1 and I2.</para>
<para>This is a very hard problem in general, so we use domain-specific knowledge that we only ever check for equivalence between blocks sharing a single immediate successor that is common, and when determining if I1 == I2 we will have already determined that next(I1) == next(I2). This inductive property allows us to simply return the value number of the next instruction that defines memory. </para>
